     1,
     "<div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">When running mediation (WLSMV/Theta) including binary outcome. I followed this approach to convert the probit coefficients to ORs. </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>model &lt;- ’<span style=\"font-size:12pt\">ciguse ˜ c*intervention </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> + </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">                              </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">b*intention</span></p>\r\n<p>                              intention ˜ a*intervention</p>\r\n<p># label threshold for ciguse</p>\r\n<p>ciguse | b0*t1</p>\r\n<p>probit11 := (-b0+c+b*a)/sqrt(bˆ2+1)</p>\r\n<p>probit10 := (-b0+c )/sqrt(bˆ2+1)</p>\r\n<p>probit00 := (-b0 )/sqrt(bˆ2+1)</p>\r\n<p>indirect := pnorm(probit11) - pnorm(probit10)</p>\r\n<p>direct := pnorm(probit10) - pnorm(probit00)</p>\r\n<p>OR.indirect := (pnorm(probit11)/(1-pnorm(probit11)))/ <span style=\"font-size:12pt\">(pnorm(probit10)/(1-pnorm(probit10)))</span></p>\r\n<p>OR.direct := (pnorm(probit10)/(1-pnorm(probit10)))/ <span style=\"font-size:12pt\">(pnorm(probit00)/(1-pnorm(probit00)))</span></p></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I noticed the p-values were not matching the CIs when obtained with the code. I thought it might be because lavaan was testing based on an the null hypothesis that the coefficient equals zero (H₀: β = 0), which might not hold for OR since the null is OR = 1.</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">When I changed from calculating OR to log odds, the results of pvalue were matching the CI of ORs. </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I got the same results when I created hypothesis tests that subtract 1 from each odds ratio, effectively testing H₀: OR - 1 = 0, which is mathematically equivalent to testing H₀: OR = 1. </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I am not sure, why i had to go over this loop, and why lavaan did not automatically set the approrpriate null. </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Or if i am missing something. </div>"
    ]
